TEXT 6392 -552 Left 2 !.inc library.mod
TEXT 6392 -592 Left 2 !.tran 0 50u 0 2n
TEXT 5512 -992 Left 6 ;PART 4 Voltage to pulse width converter
TEXT 6384 -632 Left 2 !.step param vref 1.5 3.1 0.4
TEXT 7304 -600 Left 2 ;NAND+Inv = AND we do  clk2 and Vout_comp_inv to know when\n we switch  ( the pulse detect each threshold of voltage)
TEXT 5888 -1280 Left 2 ;Minimum-size transistors are used in the digital logic to reduce\n area, because they only drive small capacitive loads. The PMOS \ndevices in the logic are made slightly wider than the NMOS devices \nto compensate for the lower hole mobility.\n\nThe comparator transistors are made much wider, W = 20um, to \nincrease transconductance and gain. This gives a sharper transition \nwhen Vtime crosses Vref and reduces pulse-width error.\n\nC3 is chosen from the required slope. The assignment requires 1.8V \nto correspond to 4.5us, so the ramp slope must be 0.4V/us. With \nIref = 1uA, this gives C3 = I/slope = 1uA / 0.4V/us = 2.5pF.
TEXT 5544 -896 Left 5 ;Laurent Béguelin 514238
TEXT 5848 -808 Left 2 ;- clk2 is the timing clock.\n- The voltage source has 10 kOhm series resistance to satisfy the source constraint.\n- When clk2 is low, Vtime is reset to VDD.\n- When clk2 is high, Vtime is discharged by the current source.
TEXT 5272 -184 Left 2 ;- C3 is charged to VDD when clk2 is low by PMOS M1.\n- When clk2 is high, M1 turns off and M30 \ndischarges C3 with approximately 1 uA.\n- Ramp equation:\n- Vtime(t) = VDD - (Iref/C3)*t\n- With Iref = 1 uA and C3 = 2.5 pF:\n- dV/dt = 0.4 V/us
TEXT 5888 432 Left 2 ;- The comparator detects when the falling ramp Vtime crosses Vref.\n-Before the crossing, Vtime > Vref.\n-At the crossing, the comparator changes state and stops the PWM pulse.\n*\n- The comparator transistors use W = 20 um to increase gm and gain.\n- This gives a sharper transition and reduces pulse-width error.
TEXT 6624 -40 Left 2 ;- This inverter turns the comparator output\n into a clean logic signal.\n- The PMOS is made wider to restore a strong\n high level and compensate for lower hole mobility.
RECTANGLE Normal 7148 -508 8320 600 2
